# cv_sample Lab Rule

Python image-processing lab for verifying/developing **algorithms**, **models**, and visual **effects**.

## Layout

- `sources/` — input images only (never overwrite)
- `code/<experiment>/` — one folder per experiment; scripts live here
- `code/<experiment>/output/` — generated results
- `code/<experiment>/weights/` — model checkpoints (do not commit large binaries)

## Agent behavior

1. Read `.cursor/skills/cv-sample-lab/SKILL.md` before adding experiments.
2. For classical CV → also use `computer-vision-opencv` / `image-processing` skills.
3. For Torch / local HF models → use `pytorch-patterns` / `huggingface-local-models`.
4. Prefer Context7 MCP for up-to-date OpenCV / PyTorch / Transformers API docs.
5. New work always gets a new `code/<name>/` folder; keep scripts runnable with plain `python`.
